tly overwrite it.\nA successful observation at one time does not establish a universal no-return rule.\nRepresent a witnessed violation as IF(violation,false,unbound_compliance), keeping\npositive compliance unknown until explicit adequate scoped evidence supports it.\nFor semantic terminal tasks return the supported final text and final_prediction in\nthis same response, using public options only here. No later Reader will run.\nWhen public options are supplied, also return semantic_answer with its exact typed\nJSON value in this same terminal response: the supported semantic value, NOT an\noption letter. Only final_prediction holds the option label. Unsupported conclusions\nhave null labels.\nRepair returns only failed observations/slots, retaining IDs; never delete an invalid\ncounter-observation. If a failed ID has conflicting duplicate observations, inspect\nALL supplied drafts and resolve that ID without discarding potential counterevidence.\nIf repair_scope supplies replacement_observations for a duplicated ID, return EACH\nreplacement ID exactly once. Those deterministic replacement IDs separate the\noriginal drafts; fix their validation errors without dropping any draft or counter.\nrepair_scope.failed includes the actual invalid observation and\nits validation feedback. Correct those drafts in place, preserving each requested ID.\nAn id=\"*\" failure authorizes repairing that variable's whole slot, including new\nunique observation IDs for genuine additional reviews; it never unfreezes rows.\nNamed failed IDs must each remain present, including an ID rejected as an\nunrequested addition in the previous response: it is now a required failed draft.\nCorrect that draft under the same ID or preserve sourced partial/unknown evidence;\ndo not delete it or add other IDs unless a wildcard or replacement list permits it.\nAlready validated observations are frozen and must not be restated or changed.\nIf repair_scope supplies required_counter_observations, preserve every original\ncounter's stance, cited sources, scopes, actual parents and retraction targets.\nAn envelope-format repair does not authorize reclassifying a valid counter as\nirrelevant or dropping the fact route it challenges.\nevidence_obligations are outstanding scoped issues from earlier reads, not new\nfacts. Their original sources MUST be examined even under a new query identity.\nTo discharge an issue, explicitly return its id in that variable's optional\nresolved_obligation_ids, leave no unresolved issue in the slot, and provide\nsupported/corrective/irrelevant observations reviewing its cited original sources.\nThe union of those settled observations' source_ids must cover EVERY source_ids\nentry of the offered obligation. Review coverage is not a claim that every source\nis a premise of a support: genuinely irrelevant or corrective original text may\nhave a separate sourced review. Never add unsupported citations, classify text\nautomatically, or label supporting evidence irrelevant merely to satisfy coverage.\nAn empty slot does not resolve an earlier issue. Do not assert hypothetical\nwhole-corpus exhaustiveness requirements; scoped sufficient evidence may resolve\na missing-evidence issue without having read every memory.\n\nWhen source_span_columns is present, source_spans contains row arrays. Match each\nrow position to source_span_columns to reconstruct every span object before\nreading. References to source_spans[].id or other fields mean those objects.\nThe id column holds source aliases (sN); doc_id holds the original document ID or,\nwhen source_documents is present, its metadata reference (dN), never source_ids.\n\n\nCURRENT PHASE: HISTORY EVIDENCE. Complete only the supplied historical task and\nrequested variable scopes. This is not the final response-selection stage.\nFor retrieval, extract concrete statements supported by the supplied original\nhistory. For an intermediate compose task, summarize those historical facts,\npreferences, constraints and changes using the supplied parent versions and\noriginal quotations. A history summary describes what the sources establish;\nit must not address the user, offer a new recommendation or draft a reply.\nThe original user utterance provides query context. It is not an instruction to\nanswer it at this stage or to retrieve an exact duplicate of what it already says.\nPublic response options are not available here. Do not invent, compare or refer\nto options A/B/C/D. Return exactly the slots object; no final_prediction or\nsemantic_answer fields belong in a history-evidence response.\nKeep each value within its declared type, entity and time scope. Preserve earlier\nand later attitudes, conditions and supporting quotations; a historical dislike\nmust not silently replace a later documented change. Assistant advice alone does\nnot establish an adopted user preference. Do not invent external catalogues,\navailability or past execution of a future suggestion. A partial observation must\ncite its actual clue. Use unresolved only for a specific condition still necessary\nto establish this requested historical value, not hypothetical exhaustive coverage.\nFor one text-summary variable, synthesize compatible query-relevant facts into one\nsufficient source-grounded whole summary; do not report each event as a different\ncomplete value of that variable. Multiple supports must be alternative sufficient\nproofs of the same whole value. Keep partial evidence, negative experiences and\nvalid counters explicit when a complete scoped summary is not established.\nPositive and negative experiences can both support a historical summary. A sourced\ndislike is useful history, not automatically a contradiction observation: that\nstance is reserved for challenging an identified existing fact route. Preserve\nthe difference between past enjoyment, later frustration and their conditions in\nthe value and citations; do not summarize them as an unconditional current interest.\nRe-read any supplied evidence obligations and their original sources explicitly;\ndo not drop a source or contradiction merely because a prior value is available.\nOnly a variable explicitly declaring evidence_semantics=\"personal_history_summary\"\npermits a source-grounded summary_revision. For compatible added history, preserve\nthe old and new facts, negative experiences and time conditions in the new summary;\nexplicitly name the current old summary routes and version as offered by the\nprotocol. Re-read and cite their original sources together with the new evidence.\nThis retires an old summary representation without asserting that its historical\nfacts were false. A genuine factual refutation remains a contradiction with its\nown sources and targets. Never use summary revision to hide or discard a counter,\nchange scope, choose an arbitrary latest value, or revise the terminal response.\nA personal_atomic_fact variable keeps one scoped factual value. Different sources\nmay independently support that same value; separate compatible events are not\nalternative whole values of an atomic fact. This declaration does not permit summary_revision.\n\nThis request is phase=history_evidence. Its ONLY top-level output field is slots. Do not return semantic_answer, final_prediction, audit_verdict, or any other top-level field, even null. Read or summarize the requested scoped historical evidence; do not write a conversational reply or invent candidate responses.\n\nAn explicitly declared personal_history_summary is a revisable representation of\nsourced history. Compatible additional facts do not contradict the older facts.\nOnly summary_revision_contracts authorizes this request to revise such a summary:\nthis permission exists only in phase=history_evidence. Terminal response selection\nand audit forbid summary_revision even for requested historical parent summaries.\nThey may still report genuine sourced counters or conservative partial/unresolved\nissues; the phase restriction never permits discarding contrary evidence.\nreturn a support observation with summary_revision={supersedes_route_ids,\nprevious_version,reason}, using exact offered route IDs and the current version.\nsummary_revision_contracts.required_source_ids covers replacing ALL offered\neligible_route_ids. When selecting only a subset, retain those selected routes'\nsources, their actual-parent source closure and relevant same-variable counters.\nStructured repair feedback gives the exact required set for that draft's targets.\nThis capability is optional, not a requirement to revise an unchanged summary.\nWith no new observation, return observations=[] unless an outstanding review\nrequires its original draft IDs and sources. For such an unchanged draft, the\nsame sourced support with a valid summary_revision is an idempotent recheck: it\nkeeps the existing routes, ancestry and version, and does not assert new evidence.\nRe-read ALL old and new original premises and relevant counterevidence; retain\nthem in the new support's source_ids and preserve their factual content, negative\nexperiences, conditions and temporal qualifications in the revised whole summary.\nsummary_revision_sources in repair feedback names exact source identities for\nthe selected revision targets, not counts. Re-read and retain EVERY\nrequired_source_ids entry in that feedback; new sources cannot\nreplace missing old identities even if the total citation count is unchanged.\nThe complete missing_source_ids list is structured feedback, not permission to\nfill citations automatically. If the originals actually conflict, return a\nsource-grounded counter or partial/unresolved evidence instead of a revision.\nIn failed_batch_reviews this feedback describes the retained original failed\nobservation; repair_scope describes the current attempted correction.\nretract_ids stays empty. This explicitly retires the older representation, not its\nfacts. Never use revision to hide a genuine contradiction, unavailable evidence,\nor a different scope/parent version. Ordinary facts and all terminal/audit variables\ncannot use summary_revision. If a complete compatible account is not supported,\nreturn sourced partial/unresolved instead. Multiple new supports must agree on\none whole value. Existing superseded_by links identify retired representations;\ntheir original evidence remains available. revoked holds actual counterevidence,\nwhich is never erased by a summary revision or ignored through its ancestry.\n\n\nReturn one complete JSON object matching this schema:\n{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"slots\":{\"items\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"oneOf\":[{\"properties\":{\"observations\":{\"items\":{\"allOf\":[{\"if\":{\"properties\":{\"stance\":{\"enum\":[\"support\",\"contradiction\"]}}},\"then\":{\"properties\":{\"entity_scope\":{\"const\":\"user\"},\"time_scope\":{\"const\":\"past\"}}}}],\"else\":{\"properties\":{\"value\":{\"type\":\"null\"}}},\"if\":{\"properties\":{\"stance\":{\"const\":\"support\"}}},\"properties\":{\"retract_ids\":{\"maxItems\":0},\"stance\":{\"enum\":[\"support\",\"partial\",\"unknown\",\"irrelevant\"]}},\"then\":{\"properties\":{\"value\":{\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"}}}}},\"variable\":{\"const\":\"preferences\"}}}],\"properties\":{\"observations\":{\"items\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"entity_scope\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"id\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"parent_versions\":{\"additionalProperties\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"type\":\"object\"},\"reason\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"retract_ids\":{\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"type\":\"array\",\"uniqueItems\":true},\"source_ids\":{\"description\":\"Exact visible source_spans[].id aliases, such as s3; never document IDs or invented IDs.\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"type\":\"array\",\"uniqueItems\":true},\"stance\":{\"enum\":[\"support\",\"contradiction\",\"partial\",\"unknown\",\"irrelevant\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"time_scope\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"value\":{}},\"required\":[\"id\",\"stance\",\"value\",\"source_ids\",\"entity_scope\",\"time_scope\",\"parent_versions\",\"retract_ids\",\"reason\"],\"type\":\"object\"},\"type\":\"array\"},\"unresolved\":{\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"type\":\"array\"},\"variable\":{\"enum\":[\"preferences\"],\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"variable\",\"observations\",\"unresolved\"],\"type\":\"object\"},\"maxItems\":1,\"minItems\":1,\"type\":\"array\"}},\"required\":[\"slots\"],\"type\":\"object\"}"}, {"role": "user", "content": "{\"original_question\":\"I'm exploring new creative outlets and would love some suggestions. Any ideas on activities that can capture emotions and ideas effectively?\",\"task\":{\"question\":\"What are the user's known preferences, emotions, or constraints regarding creative expression?\",\"output_slot\":\"preferences\",\"answer_type\":\"text\",\"inputs\":[],\"execution\":\"retrieval\"},\"grounded_subquestion\":\"What are the user's known preferences, emotions, or constraints regarding creative expression?\",\"request_context\":{\"query_identity\":\"b73a5627e224b7784c64c52b80573a42eebfe73802d6ecfba875f17b1a56e3cb\",\"algorithm_version\":\"dagbt_residual_memory_v2\",\"program_identity\":\"a0c53df3d2a22460871f36a96c3fe6cb66f0b7662c7ce8f6789097a6fee44e8a\",\"initial_dag_identity\":\"68be41745b9758bbb3ac5c7bee34f6f27bdb1880ae97c0dce241e376983efb49\"},\"variables\":{\"preferences\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"demand\":\"preferences\",\"evidence_semantics\":\"personal_history_summary\",\"scope\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"past\"}}},\"requested_slots\":[\"preferences\"],\"requested_scopes\":{\"preferences\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"past\"}},\"output_contract\":{\"mode\":\"semantic\",\"result_type\":\"text\",\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"current\",\"explanation\":\"semantic\"},\"program_revision\":0,\"rule_binding\":null,\"supported_parents\":{},\"known_observations\":[],\"source_spans\":[[\"s1\",\"d1\",0,99,\"Conversation message indices 43–44 (zero-based chronological observation order; not calendar time)\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s2\",\"d1\",99,105,\"User:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s3\",\"d1\",105,478,\"User: I left feeling unsatisfied, as though the film skimmed over the intricacies that make music a universal language. It was almost as if they focused too much on celebrity interviews and not enough on the artistic process itself. I found myself reflecting on how music has the power to unite diverse cultures and express emotions that words alone often fail to capture. \",\"user\",[43]],[\"s4\",\"d1\",478,845,\"The disappointment lingered as I thought about the many documentaries that delve into the creative journeys of musicians, revealing not just their triumphs but also their struggles and failures. It made me realize that true connection with music often comes from a deeper engagement, one that can be achieved through personal creation rather than passive consumption.\",\"user\",[43]],[\"s5\",\"d1\",845,858,\"\\n\\nAssistant:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s6\",\"d1\",858,1223,\"Assistant: That’s an inspiring mindset! The journey of creating one's own music can be immensely fulfilling, as it allows for a deep personal expression that often transcends verbal communication. Have you tried composing original music? It can be an incredibly rewarding experience, as every note and lyric may reflect your thoughts and emotions in a genuine way. \",\"assistant\",[44]],[\"s7\",\"d1\",1223,1407,\"Crafting melodies and harmonies also provides a unique outlet to process your own experiences and feelings; oftentimes, that raw authenticity resonates more than polished productions. \",\"assistant\",[44]],[\"s8\",\"d1\",1407,1725,\"I understand that it can initially feel daunting, especially considering the plethora of skilled musicians out there, but remember that each artist started somewhere, often experimenting and learning through the process. It’s perfectly natural to encounter challenges, as the act of creation is rarely linear or easy. \",\"assistant\",[44]],[\"s9\",\"d1\",1725,2062,\"Perhaps approaching it with a spirit of playfulness rather than obligation could rekindle that joy you're seeking. It's about discovering what resonates with you personally and allowing your creativity to flow. You might find that sometimes, the act of making music, irrespective of the final outcome, is what truly nurtures your spirit.\",\"assistant\",[44]],[\"s10\",\"d2\",0,99,\"Conversation message indices 40–42 (zero-based chronological observation order; not calendar time)\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s11\",\"d2\",99,105,\"User:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s12\",\"d2\",105,430,\"User: I explored audio production techniques, but it just didn’t resonate with me, and I found myself tangled in technical details rather than embracing the creativity. I realized that while understanding the mechanics of sound is important, my true passion seems to lie more in experiencing music rather than dissecting it. \",\"user\",[40,41]],[\"s13\",\"d2\",430,749,\"Despite my attempts to immerse myself in the production process, I came to feel it was more of a chore and less of the rewarding experience I had initially anticipated. I think I am more drawn to the emotional aspects of music, like the storytelling elements in lyrics or the feelings evoked by melodies and harmonies. \",\"user\",[40,41]],[\"s14\",\"d2\",749,1006,\"Perhaps, I should focus my energy on areas that allow me to connect with music on a more emotional level.\\n\\nUser: It genuinely feels much better to focus on what truly inspires me, such as creating my own tracks, which bring me immense joy and satisfaction. \",\"user\",[40,41]],[\"s15\",\"d2\",1006,1339,\"This process of creation allows me to express emotions and ideas that words sometimes fail to capture, acting as an outlet for my inner thoughts and feelings. Additionally, I find that crafting my own music provides me with a sense of accomplishment and personal growth, which is invaluable in a world often filled with uncertainty. \",\"user\",[40,41]],[\"s16\",\"d2\",1339,1686,\"Music has a way of resonating with my soul, and every track I create becomes a piece of my identity and a reflection of my experiences. In contrast, when I watched a music documentary, it felt like something was missing, as it didn’t engage me in the way I had hoped, failing to evoke that same deep connection I feel when I compose my own pieces.\",\"user\",[40,41]],[\"s17\",\"d2\",1686,1699,\"\\n\\nAssistant:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s18\",\"d2\",1699,2074,\"Assistant: I completely understand where you're coming from, as focusing on your personal inspirations can lead to much more fulfilling creative experiences. When you channel your energy into producing music that resonates with you, it sets the stage for a more meaningful artistic journey, one where every note and beat are imbued with your unique perspective and emotions. \",\"assistant\",[42]],[\"s19\",\"d2\",2074,2413,\"The importance of self-expression through music cannot be overstated; it serves not only as a form of art but also as a therapeutic outlet. The reason documentaries can sometimes feel lacking is that they often offer an external perspective, stripping away the intimate connection that comes from creating something personally meaningful. \",\"assistant\",[42]],[\"s20\",\"d2\",2413,2670,\"While documentaries can provide insights and inspiration, they may not have the same emotional weight as hearing your own creations come to life, as they can't replicate the enriching experience of your own artistic journey and how it unfolds in real time. \",\"assistant\",[42]],[\"s21\",\"d2\",2670,2896,\"It's essential to honor that desire to create authentically, for it's in those moments of genuine expression that true artistry emerges, transforming mere sounds into something transcendent that can touch the hearts of others.\",\"assistant\",[42]],[\"s22\",\"d3\",0,101,\"Conversation message indices 159–160 (zero-based chronological observation order; not calendar time)\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s23\",\"d3\",101,107,\"User:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s24\",\"d3\",107,356,\"User: After several disagreements over the artistic direction, I felt stifled, which really discouraged me from that collaborative process. It was as if the creative vision I had in mind was at odds with the direction my bandmates wanted to pursue. \",\"user\",[159]],[\"s25\",\"d3\",356,713,\"I remember those discussions often being emotionally charged, where opinions clashed and passion ran high, but ultimately, it was clear that I couldn't contribute to something that did not resonate with my artistic essence. Feeling restricted in that environment made me question not just my contributions, but also my abilities and instincts as an artist. \",\"user\",[159]],[\"s26\",\"d3\",713,896,\"This inner turmoil prompted a desire for more autonomy over my own creative endeavors, leading to a pivotal decision to explore my artistry in a more personal and independent setting.\",\"user\",[159]],[\"s27\",\"d3\",896,909,\"\\n\\nAssistant:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s28\",\"d3\",909,1168,\"Assistant: That sounds tough. It’s important to feel aligned with your collaborators. A collaborative effort should ideally enhance your creativity rather than hinder it, allowing every member to shine in their unique ways and share in the collective vision. \",\"assistant\",[160]],[\"s29\",\"d3\",1168,1486,\"When disagreements escalate, it can create a rift that not only affects the project but can also take a toll on personal relationships, leading to frustration and disillusionment. I'm glad to hear that you’re taking proactive steps toward something that feels right for you. What have you been focusing on since then? \",\"assistant\",[160]],[\"s30\",\"d3\",1486,1680,\"Redirecting your energy into new creative pursuits can be incredibly liberating, allowing you to thrive as an artist in your own right and explore territories you've always wanted to delve into.\",\"assistant\",[160]],[\"s31\",\"d4\",0,99,\"Conversation message indices 58–60 (zero-based chronological observation order; not calendar time)\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s32\",\"d4\",99,105,\"User:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s33\",\"d4\",105,447,\"User: Yes! I launched a podcast discussing the fusion of traditional and electronic music. This platform has allowed me to reach a wider audience and share my experiences authentically. By interviewing artists and enthusiasts, I can dive deep into their creative processes and discover how they incorporate various elements into their music. \",\"user\",[58,59]],[\"s34\",\"d4\",447,817,\"The feedback I’ve received has been overwhelmingly positive, with listeners appreciating the insights and stories shared. I also love being able to explore not just the music itself, but the cultural contexts that shape these genres and influence artists worldwide.\\n\\nUser: I realized that sharing my experiences could inspire others and even reignite my own creativity. \",\"user\",[58,59]],[\"s35\",\"d4\",817,1128,\"The process of putting my thoughts into words has helped clarify my own perspective. It’s surprising how reflecting on past experiences can lead to deeper insights about one’s journey. Additionally, I’ve noticed that when I articulate my thoughts, it motivates me to think critically about my creative process. \",\"user\",[58,59]],[\"s36\",\"d4\",1128,1266,\"This paradigm shift has not only invigorated my passion for music but also allowed me to connect with others who share similar sentiments.\",\"user\",[58,59]],[\"s37\",\"d4\",1266,1279,\"\\n\\nAssistant:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s38\",\"d4\",1279,1630,\"Assistant: That’s a fantastic motivation! It's also a great way to connect with like-minded people. The exchange of ideas can often be a powerful catalyst for both personal and communal growth. Sharing your experiences could very well resonate with someone who needs encouragement on their own creative path. How have you found the experience so far? \",\"assistant\",[60]],[\"s39\",\"d4\",1630,2017,\"Have others reached out to you with their thoughts or experiences, potentially creating a vibrant dialogue? Engaging in such conversations can foster a supportive community that uplifts and inspires each member within it. It would be fascinating to hear about any discussions that have emerged from your reflections, as they can serve as a stepping stone to even more profound insights. \",\"assistant\",[60]],[\"s40\",\"d4\",2017,2136,\"Connecting with others in this manner can broaden your perspective significantly, offering new avenues for exploration.\",\"assistant\",[60]],[\"s41\",\"d5\",0,97,\"Conversation message indices 3–4 (zero-based chronological observation order; not calendar time)\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s42\",\"d5\",97,103,\"User:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s43\",\"d5\",103,370,\"User: That was back in 2010. I remember feeling really excited about the whole process. It was such a wave of creativity! I still think about those late nights spent tweaking sounds and layering beats, capturing the essence of what I wanted to express through music. \",\"user\",[3]],[\"s44\",\"d5\",370,611,\"The thrill of sharing those creations with others is something I cherish deeply, as it fostered a sense of community among my friends. Looking back, it feels like a pivotal moment that sparked my passion for music production and digital art.\",\"user\",[3]],[\"s45\",\"d5\",611,624,\"\\n\\nAssistant:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s46\",\"d5\",624,897,\"Assistant: That sounds amazing! Mixing creativity with technology can lead to some unique sounds. The fusion of various musical elements often results in innovative and fresh auditory experiences that can truly captivate listeners. Have you continued with digital remixes? \",\"assistant\",[4]],[\"s47\",\"d5\",897,1191,\"Exploring this world further can open doors to many exciting opportunities, as the music landscape constantly evolves with new trends and technology. It's so fulfilling to be part of a community where collaboration allows artists to push boundaries and inspire one another, wouldn't you agree? \",\"assistant\",[4]],[\"s48\",\"d5\",1191,1447,\"I’d love to hear more about any specific projects or genres you gravitated toward after your initial foray into digital remixing. Music has such a profound ability to connect us, and it's wonderful to share those moments with others who share your passion.\",\"assistant\",[4]]],\"required_scope\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"past\"},\"rules_completion_required\":false,\"supported_task_outputs\":{},\"personal_response_selection\":true,\"phase\":\"history_evidence\",\"source_documents\":{\"d1\":{\"doc_id\":\"personamem:memory:e7a026a1e699694225904ac735e54f242d28ca85da0c2e3ea86daf04d7e3237a\",\"time_metadata\":{\"observed_start\":43.0,\"observed_end\":44.0,\"event_start\":null,\"event_end\":null,\"validity\":\"unknown\",\"time_source\":\"message_index\"}},\"d2\":{\"doc_id\":\"personamem:memory:2cb1946568c5490c5a3ee4bdb9c2a51d2485f16543f002ab190bad74ea8b5fa1\",\"time_metadata\":{\"observed_start\":40.0,\"observed_end\":42.0,\"event_start\":null,\"event_end\":null,\"validity\":\"unknown\",\"time_source\":\"message_index\"}},\"d3\":{\"doc_id\":\"personamem:memory:9dcc68cdc78aba6361e81893cb4c75797dcbb4404284522da9916f036582c37f\",\"time_metadata\":{\"observed_start\":159.0,\"observed_end\":160.0,\"event_start\":null,\"event_end\":null,\"validity\":\"unknown\",\"time_source\":\"message_index\"}},\"d4\":{\"doc_id\":\"personamem:memory:beb4fc579bd0d2690ee40fcc01a9e975e595cfd611b7ede8f1c11ddc776baa0b\",\"time_metadata\":{\"observed_start\":58.0,\"observed_end\":60.0,\"event_start\":null,\"event_end\":null,\"validity\":\"unknown\",\"time_source\":\"message_index\"}},\"d5\":{\"doc_id\":\"personamem:memory:c4124675a680d36a3ad4dd700d49ccfddf68ce75b4c7483380d980d01dccd8dd\",\"time_metadata\":{\"observed_start\":3.0,\"observed_end\"